 "answer_verbatim": "There isn’t one objectively “best” orthodontist for everyone—the right choice depends on your case, location, budget, and whether you prefer braces or aligners. Based on the available information, **Walnut Central Orthodontics** is one Dallas practice worth comparing: it offers braces and Invisalign, and its listing reports board-certified orthodontists and a strong review record. **Ellis Orthodontics** is another option, particularly if you want a smaller private practice; it offers braces and clear aligners and is listed as board-certified.\n\nBefore choosing, book two or three consultations and ask each orthodontist to explain your treatment options, expected timeline, total cost (including retainers and refinements), and who will supervise your care. Confirm credentials and recent reviews independently, too.",
